# Copy to `.env.local` and fill in.

# --- Sanity CMS ---------------------------------------------------------
# Optional. Sanity now holds only editorial extras — show dates, the hero
# image, and per-album blurbs. Album and track metadata comes from Deezer, so
# the site builds and renders without these.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_ values are exposed to the browser, so they are not secrets.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SANITY_PROJECT_ID=6y0e37tr
NEXT_PUBLIC_SANITY_DATASET=production

# --- Deezer -------------------------------------------------------------
# No credentials of any kind. https://api.deezer.com is public: no API key, no
# OAuth, no account. The artist id lives in src/data/site.js
# (DEEZER_ARTIST_ID = 77304962), not here, because it is not a secret and not
# environment-specific.

# --- Spotify ------------------------------------------------------------
# No credentials either. Spotify is used only for its embed iframe, which is
# public. The Web API is deliberately NOT used: since Feb 2026 it requires the
# app owner to hold an active Premium subscription, returns null preview_url
# under Client Credentials, and dropped /artists/{id}/top-tracks.
#
# Per-album Spotify ids are optional content, not config — set them in Sanity
# (`spotifyAlbumId`) or in SPOTIFY_ALBUM_IDS in src/lib/albums.js. Releases
# without one fall back to the Deezer widget automatically.
